#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Steps to Solve by Factorizing 📊]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[1️⃣ Arrange the equation in standard form]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[2️⃣ Factor the left side of the equation]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[3️⃣ Set each factor to zero]
#v(20pt)
#only("4-")[4️⃣ Solve the resulting linear equations]

#only("1")[
#voiceover("The first step in solving a quadratic equation by factorizing is to arrange it in standard form. This means having all terms on one side, typically the left, and zero on the other side.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("Next, we factor the left side of the equation. This involves finding two or more expressions that, when multiplied together, give us our original expression.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("Once we've factored, we set each factor to zero. This is based on the zero product property, which states that if the product of factors is zero, at least one of the factors must be zero.")
]
#only("4")[
#voiceover("Finally, we solve the resulting linear equations to find our solutions or roots.")
]
]


#slide()[
